  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"1.4.0\"\n  lib_version: \"0.1.0.dev\"\n\nrecipe:\n  name: ghostty\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://release.files.ghostty.org/${{ version }}/ghostty-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: cb188ac6c3a8278d5fd7bfef15d8c017104c87f638b5560eb38024a71ae0f005\n  patches:\n    # Build-time executables must use the conda sysroot glibc target too.\n    - patches/build-glibc-version.patch\n    # Keep the existing headless-macOS icon compiler workaround.\n    - patches/drop-iconcomposer-icon.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip: target_platform not in [\"linux-64\", \"linux-aarch64\", \"osx-arm64\", \"osx-64\", \"win-64\"]\n\noutputs:\n  - package:\n      name: ghostty\n    build:\n      number: 0\n      dynamic_linking:\n        # On osx we ship a self-contained .app bundle with Sparkle.framework\n        # inside Contents/Frameworks/. xcodebuild emits the standard\n        # @rpath = @executable_path/../Frameworks for that case. Without\n        # this opt-out, rattler-build's binary relocator rewrites the\n        # rpath to @executable_path/../../../../lib (conda's standard\n        # lib/), which breaks Sparkle loading at launch:\n        #   dyld: Library not loaded: @rpath/Sparkle.framework/...\n        #         tried: $PREFIX/lib/Sparkle.framework/... (no such file)\n        # We express this as a conditional allowlist instead of `false`:\n        #   - linux: [\"**\"]  → relocate everything (default behaviour)\n        #   - osx:   []      → relocate nothing\n        # If a future maintainer adds a conda host dep on macOS the\n        # resulting binary won't have its rpath rewritten and the test\n        # will fail with \"image not found\" — which is the right signal\n        # to come back and tighten this list.\n        binary_relocation:\n          - if: linux\n            then: \"**\"\n      # Platform support, current state:\n      #   - linux-64: built via zig (see build.sh, linux branch).\n      #   - osx-arm64: built via xcodebuild + ad-hoc codesigning against\n      #     macos/Ghostty.xcodeproj (see build.sh, osx branch). Going native-arm\n      #     first because earlier osx-64 attempts panicked inside zig\n      #     (\"reached unreachable code\" compiling x86_64-macos.13.0 against\n      #     MacOSX15.5.sdk) — we suspected the conda-forge x86_64 zig running\n      #     under Rosetta on an Apple Silicon runner.\n      #   - osx-64: temporarily skipped. With build_platform.osx_64=osx_arm64\n      #     in conda-forge.yml the osx_64 build would cross-compile from arm64,\n      #     but we want osx-arm64 green first before opening up the cross-build.\n      #   - linux-aarch64: skipped — gtk4-layer-shell isn't packaged for it yet.\n      #   - Windows: GUI unsupported; the separate VT output builds there.\n      skip: target_platform not in [\"linux-64\", \"osx-arm64\"]\n      files:\n        include:\n          - \"**\"\n        exclude:\n          - lib/*ghostty-vt*\n          - bin/*ghostty-vt*\n          - include/ghostty/**\n          - share/pkgconfig/libghostty-vt*.pc\n      script:\n        file: build\n\n    requirements:\n      build:\n        # Ghostty 1.4.0 requires Zig 0.17.0. It is also invoked by the\n        # Xcode project's run-script phases on macOS.\n        - zig 0.17.0.*\n        # Unpack Zig 0.17 cache archives for the offline --system build.\n        - python >=3.11\n        # pandoc is invoked by ghostty's zig build to generate manpages and\n        # HTML docs on every platform — without it: \"error: failed to spawn\n        # and capture stdio from pandoc: FileNotFound\".\n        - pandoc\n        - if: linux\n          then:\n            - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n            - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n            - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n            - pkg-config\n            - gettext\n            - libxml2\n            - gobject-introspection\n            - wayland-protocols\n        # macOS: xcodebuild is system-provided on the conda-forge osx_arm64\n        # runner. Additional macOS-only build deps to be discovered via CI.\n      host:\n        - if: linux\n          then:\n            # GTK / GUI\n            - gtk4\n            - libadwaita\n            - gtk4-layer-shell\n            - libxkbcommon\n            - wayland\n            - xorg-libx11\n            - xorg-libxcursor\n            - xorg-libxi\n            - xorg-libxrandr\n            - libgl-devel\n            - gst-plugins-base\n            - gst-plugins-good\n            - gstreamer\n            # System libraries linked dynamically by zig build's\n            # systemIntegrationOption defaults on Linux.\n            - bzip2\n            - expat\n            - fontconfig\n            - freetype\n            - harfbuzz\n            - libpng\n            - libxml2\n            - oniguruma\n            - zlib\n        # macOS host deps live inside the .app bundle (Sparkle, Swift libs)\n        # or come from the system SDK. Start empty; tighten once CI is green.\n      run:\n        - if: linux\n          then:\n            # gtk4-layer-shell doesn't export a run-export, so the .so.0 needs to\n            # be listed explicitly (otherwise: \"ghostty: error while loading shared\n            # libraries: libgtk4-layer-shell.so.0\").\n            - gtk4-layer-shell\n            # GStreamer is dlopened at runtime for video/audio integrations.\n            - gst-plugins-base\n            - gst-plugins-good\n            - gstreamer\n        # macOS run deps: bundled inside Ghostty.app — none required from conda.\n\n    tests:\n      - script:\n          - ghostty --version\n          - ghostty +help\n      - package_contents:\n          bin:\n            - ghostty\n          files:\n            - Menu/ghostty.json\n            - if: linux\n              then:\n                - share/applications/com.mitchellh.ghostty.desktop\n                # ghostty installs its terminfo as the canonical xterm-ghostty entry\n                # (with a relative symlink ghostty -> xterm-ghostty that conda strips\n                # and we recreate in build.sh).\n                - share/terminfo/78/xterm-ghostty\n                - share/terminfo/x/xterm-ghostty\n            - if: osx\n              then:\n                - Applications/Ghostty.app/Contents/MacOS/ghostty\n                - Applications/Ghostty.app/Contents/Info.plist\n                # Assets.car is the compiled asset catalog (icons, etc.). On\n                # earlier runs xcodebuild's ibtoold sub-tool crashed during\n                # CompileAssetCatalogVariant — printed \"BUILD FAILED\" but the\n                # overall build still appeared to succeed. Listing it here so\n                # if it's ever missing the package_contents test catches it\n                # instead of silently shipping an iconless bundle.\n                - Applications/Ghostty.app/Contents/Resources/Assets.car\n                - Applications/Ghostty.app/Contents/Resources/AppIcon.icns\n  - package:\n      name: libghostty-vt\n      version: ${{ lib_version }}\n    about:\n      summary: Ghostty VT parsing library with a C API\n      description: Standalone terminal sequence parsing library, without the Ghostty GUI.\n    build:\n      number: 0\n      skip: target_platform not in [\"linux-64\", \"linux-aarch64\", \"osx-arm64\", \"osx-64\", \"win-64\"]\n      script:\n        interpreter: python\n        file: build-lib.py\n    requirements:\n      # The experimental 0.1 C ABI may change between Ghostty releases.\n      run_exports:\n        - ${{ pin_subpackage('libghostty-vt', exact=True) }}\n      build:\n        - zig 0.17.0.*\n        - python >=3.11\n        - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n        - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    tests:\n      - package_contents:\n          include:\n            - ghostty/vt.h\n            - ghostty/vt/osc.h\n          files:\n            - if: unix\n              then:\n                - lib/pkgconfig/libghostty-vt.pc\n                - lib/pkgconfig/libghostty-vt-static.pc\n              else:\n                - Library/lib/pkgconfig/libghostty-vt.pc\n                - Library/lib/pkgconfig/libghostty-vt-static.pc\n            - if: linux\n              then:\n                - lib/libghostty-vt.so.0.1.0\n                - lib/libghostty-vt.a\n            - if: osx\n              then:\n                - lib/libghostty-vt.0.1.0.dylib\n                - lib/libghostty-vt.a\n            - if: win\n              then:\n                - Library/bin/ghostty-vt.dll\n                - Library/lib/ghostty-vt.lib\n                - Library/lib/ghostty-vt-static.lib\n      - script: python test-lib.py\n        requirements:\n          run:\n            - python >=3.11\n            - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n            - pkg-config\n        files:\n          recipe:\n            - test-lib.py\n            - test-lib.c\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://ghostty.org\n  summary: A fast, native, feature-rich terminal emulator\n  description: |\n    Ghostty is a terminal emulator that differentiates itself by being fast,\n    feature-rich, and native. While there are many excellent terminal emulators\n    available, they all force you to choose between speed, features, or native\n    UIs. Ghostty provides all three.\n  license: MIT\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  repository: https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty\n  documentation: https://ghostty.org/docs\n\nextra:\n  feedstock-name: ghostty\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - tdejager\n",
